[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5691886717","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123536#issuecomment-5691886717","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123536","id":5691886717,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU0NMfQ","user":{"login":"ParisMars","id":119086889,"node_id":"U_kgDOBxkfKQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/119086889?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars","html_url":"https://github.com/ParisMars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ParisMars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T04:07:39Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T04:07:39Z","body":"For some reason the gradient texture for the Texture2DParameter is missing when you open the zip of the project, so here's a short video of the bug:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7eb3a8b6-a968-4949-bdf8-d803b6eea25e","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5691886717/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5745343770","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123536#issuecomment-5745343770","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123536","id":5745343770,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVnL9Gg","user":{"login":"Vaatsal-source","id":229524920,"node_id":"U_kgDODa5FuA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229524920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source","html_url":"https://github.com/Vaatsal-source","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Vaatsal-source/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-19T21:13:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-19T21:21:45Z","body":"I can confirm this on a 4.8.dev build from master (commit 5902d3f37).\n\nTo reproduce I fed the UV through a centered radial distance (Length x3) into a Texture2D node with a GradientTexture1D attached directly (not a Texture2DParameter), then to Albedo. With a red-to-blue gradient, the color visibly cycles back and forth (blue - red - blue) instead of holding at the edges, which shows Repeat mode is forced on with no way to turn it off for this node.\n\n<img width=\"1917\" height=\"987\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0eeae761-a3ed-48aa-8986-838f490a5302\" />\n\nEdit : Digging into the code, the cause seems straightforward when a texture is attached directly to VisualShaderNodeTexture (rather than through a Parameter), it just generates a plain uniform sampler2D with no filter or repeat hint whatsoever , VisualShaderNodeTextureParameter, already handles this correctly with texture_filter/texture_repeat properties , A possible fix could be to add those same two properties here as well, reusing the existing get_sampler_hint() helper that already does the work","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5745343770/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]